<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The Kabmo wordmark, for the launch overlay.

  A port of `public/kabmo-wordmark.svg` — the file README.md embeds — not a
  redrawn copy: same plate, same three K strokes, same outlined word, same
  colours. Three things differ, and only because a VectorDrawable is not an
  SVG:

  1. **Every y is shifted by +128.12.** The README file is authored around a
     baseline at y=0 (its viewBox starts at -128.12), and a VectorDrawable
     viewport has no negative origin.
  2. **The plate is a path, not a `<rect>`.** VectorDrawable has no rect
     element; this is the same 156.25 tile with the same 34.18 corner radius.
  3. **The gradient is inline**, as `userSpaceOnUse` coordinates translated
     into viewport space (startX/startY/endX/endY) — which is the same
     horizontal amber-to-orange run the README file declares.

  Gradients in a VectorDrawable need API 24, which is the shell's minSdk.
  `WordmarkDrawableTest` pins this file against the README source, so the two
  cannot drift apart silently.
-->
